WEBVTT

00:02.628 --> 00:04.391
Good evening. I'm Diane Simmons.

00:04.564 --> 00:07.931
A stunning development tonight
as O.J. Simpson is proven innocent.

00:08.067 --> 00:11.093
We have the identity of the real killer.
But first...

00:11.237 --> 00:14.900
It's fall. The time of year when the leaves
turn a pretty, purpley orange...

00:15.007 --> 00:17.976
...and Quahog prepares
for its annual Harvest Festival Parade.

00:18.077 --> 00:20.602
Asian reporter Trisha Takanawa
joins us live...

00:20.713 --> 00:23.705
...from the ceremony where
they are choosing this year's theme.

00:23.816 --> 00:27.183
Diane, behind me are 1,000 beautiful doves.

00:27.320 --> 00:30.483
Gently tied to each of their delicate legs
is a parade theme...

00:30.590 --> 00:33.218
...suggested by
ordinary citizens of Quahog.

00:33.326 --> 00:35.658
And here to pick
this year's winning theme...

00:35.761 --> 00:38.161
...is Ten Commandments star,
Charlton Heston.

00:38.264 --> 00:40.323
Let my pigeons go!

00:44.170 --> 00:46.434
He nailed one! We have our theme!

00:47.740 --> 00:50.834
I submitted "togetherness."
A simple theme.

00:50.943 --> 00:52.808
But powerful, nonetheless.

00:52.912 --> 00:56.814
Come on, "overcoming adversity"!
Let's go, "overcoming adversity"!

00:56.916 --> 00:59.282
Show me "women I gave the clap to"!

00:59.485 --> 01:02.477
And the Harvest Festival Parade theme is:

01:02.588 --> 01:05.022
"The episode of Who's the Boss?

01:05.124 --> 01:07.991
"...where Tony sees Angela
naked in the shower."

01:08.094 --> 01:10.892
Yes! That's mine! Un-freaking-believable!

01:13.866 --> 01:17.734
Clumsy oaf! Michael Flatley
must be turning over in his grave.

01:18.404 --> 01:20.804
Wait a minute. He's not dead yet.

01:21.340 --> 01:22.898
"Michael Flatley."

01:23.175 --> 01:26.975
It's great they picked your theme,
but isn't it a little esoteric?

01:27.146 --> 01:28.545
Esoteric?

01:28.814 --> 01:31.180
- Could it mean "sexy"?
- I think it's a science term.

01:31.284 --> 01:33.718
Fellas, esoteric means "delicious."

01:34.353 --> 01:37.083
Who's the Boss? Is not a food.

01:37.323 --> 01:38.585
Swing and a miss.

01:39.025 --> 01:42.153
"It seems today that all you see

01:42.662 --> 01:45.790
"is violence in movies and sex on TV

01:45.965 --> 01:48.957
"But where are those good,
old-fashioned values

01:49.602 --> 01:51.695
"on which we used to rely?

01:52.638 --> 01:54.799
"Lucky there's a family guy

01:55.841 --> 01:59.174
"Lucky there's a man who'll
positively tell you

01:59.278 --> 02:00.802
"all the things that make us

02:00.913 --> 02:02.403
"laugh 'n' cry

02:02.648 --> 02:06.607
"He's a family guy"

02:09.255 --> 02:12.554
I have no friends,
and it's all because of this stupid purse!

02:12.858 --> 02:16.521
What did you do to my daughter?
I swear to God, if you touched her...

02:17.530 --> 02:18.895
Honey, what happened?

02:19.832 --> 02:21.265
It was lunchtime and...

02:21.734 --> 02:23.998
I love the color of your Prada bag.

02:24.103 --> 02:27.869
- Yeah, but yours has that great clasp.
- Hey, Meg, you want to come to lunch?

02:28.074 --> 02:32.101
You know what? There's no room
in my car for your big, ugly purse.

02:34.613 --> 02:36.911
Meg, let me tell you about popularity.

02:37.016 --> 02:39.416
Mrs. Canner? Are you coming?
Bye!

02:40.319 --> 02:43.311
Daddy, if you really loved me,
you'd buy me a Prada bag.

02:43.422 --> 02:46.550
I can't say no to you, honey.
What are they, like, $10?

02:46.659 --> 02:48.752
More like $1,100.

02:50.463 --> 02:52.727
You wish I loved you that much!

02:54.200 --> 02:56.760
We'll never finish the float
in time for the parade.

02:56.869 --> 02:58.268
Pick up the pace, guys!

02:58.371 --> 02:59.929
Peter, your theme is a dud.

03:00.039 --> 03:02.405
Yeah. I've never even seen
Who's the Boss?

03:02.541 --> 03:07.035
Tuesdays in the '80s I was always
in bed by 8:00 and home by 11:00.

03:07.646 --> 03:11.639
But I can't do it without you guys,
because I'll tell you who's the boss.

03:11.751 --> 03:13.548
It's not Tony or Angela.

03:13.652 --> 03:16.746
It's not even man-crazy Mona. It's all of us.

03:17.223 --> 03:20.590
You're the boss because you never
give up, like with the ladies.

03:20.960 --> 03:22.120
Gemini.

03:22.661 --> 03:23.787
Capricorn.

03:24.864 --> 03:26.764
I know you're not a Virgo!

03:28.834 --> 03:31.200
From down here, you look like a Pisces!

03:31.937 --> 03:35.270
And Cleveland, you're the boss
because of your attention to detail.

03:35.408 --> 03:39.208
Like when we play pool,
you take so long to line up your shots...

03:39.311 --> 03:41.575
...I just want to crack you with a cue stick.

03:41.680 --> 03:44.581
But I don't because that would be
a hate crime, and I love you.

03:44.683 --> 03:49.120
And Joe, I've had new neighbors before,
but none were half the man you are.

03:49.522 --> 03:52.047
Since you're half a man already,
that splits them...

03:52.158 --> 03:54.524
...into some kind of fraction
I can't even measure.

03:54.627 --> 03:57.790
He's right. If we work together,
we can win this thing. Who's in?

03:58.397 --> 04:00.092
Go, Spooner Street!

04:05.004 --> 04:07.495
My dad always says,
"Measure twice, cut once."

04:07.606 --> 04:10.803
My daddy always said,
"Cleveland Jr., quit jumping on the bed!"

04:12.445 --> 04:14.072
We didn't measure!

04:14.914 --> 04:17.974
Amazing. The whole
neighborhood is working together.

04:18.084 --> 04:19.745
You know what's really amazing?

04:19.852 --> 04:24.084
I haven't brushed my teeth in three days,
and no one has said a thing.

04:28.060 --> 04:30.528
If I had a job, I could buy the bag myself.

04:31.297 --> 04:34.892
I have squandered my munitions budget
on that insipid Rugrats video!

04:35.000 --> 04:36.831
Perhaps I should seek employment.

04:36.936 --> 04:39.871
Mother teaches piano.
I suppose I could as well.

04:40.372 --> 04:42.135
All right, try it again, Richard.

04:42.241 --> 04:45.142
And remember,
the wrong keys are electrified.

04:48.347 --> 04:50.076
I don't want to play the piano!

04:50.182 --> 04:52.707
Indeed.
Would you rather play the bassoon?

04:55.988 --> 04:57.922
No experience? No, thanks.

05:00.426 --> 05:02.417
Oh, nuts. Young lady.

05:02.895 --> 05:04.522
What's the little guy's name?

05:04.630 --> 05:05.619
What do you care?

05:05.731 --> 05:09.895
I can't send an unwed teenage mother
out on the street without a job.

05:10.002 --> 05:12.368
Stewie. My son's name is Stewie.

05:13.806 --> 05:17.606
Welcome to the 83rd annual
Quahog Harvest Festival Parade.

05:17.710 --> 05:19.644
Are you as excited as I am, Tom?

05:19.745 --> 05:21.679
Are you kidding, Diane? I've got wood...

05:21.780 --> 05:25.045
...and clipped onto it
is a list of this year's float entries.

05:25.151 --> 05:28.348
Remember, the float that best captures
this year's theme...

05:28.454 --> 05:30.718
...wins Quahog's coveted Golden Clam.

05:30.823 --> 05:32.313
And here's our first float.

05:32.424 --> 05:35.484
It looks like some wires
got crossed on Clover Street.

05:35.594 --> 05:38.461
That's not Angela.
That's Mona, Angela's mom.

05:38.564 --> 05:41.294
Wonderful use of tree bark
for the age spots though.

05:41.834 --> 05:44.803
This one's got Tony bathing Jonathan.
That's just plain wrong.

05:44.904 --> 05:47.964
Each float possesses its own
unique charm. But none of them...

05:48.073 --> 05:50.041
Oh, baby! Look at that!

05:51.911 --> 05:53.776
The float turned out great.

05:53.879 --> 05:57.872
Our neighborhood hasn't been this united
since Quagmire got us free cable.

06:02.254 --> 06:03.983
We are not bad people.

06:04.089 --> 06:07.616
We just don't want to pay $12 a month
for Cinemax.

06:09.929 --> 06:12.159
First place goes to Spooner Street.

06:14.400 --> 06:16.368
We won! All right!

06:29.848 --> 06:31.748
Come on now! This is damn foolish!

06:31.850 --> 06:33.545
My theme, my trophy!

06:33.652 --> 06:36.587
My aunt Fanny!
You said it yourself! I'm the boss!

06:36.689 --> 06:41.058
He said I, too, was the boss.
And it's time Cleveland got his due.

06:41.160 --> 06:43.458
Joe, my feet are starting to swell.

06:43.562 --> 06:46.292
You two go home.
I can stay here as long as it takes.

06:46.398 --> 06:49.299
You'd be amazed how little one eats
when your legs don't work.

06:49.401 --> 06:51.301
There's only one way to settle this.

06:52.137 --> 06:53.229
Russian Roulette.

06:53.339 --> 06:56.536
Three bullets, last guy standing
keeps the trophy. Me first.

06:56.842 --> 06:59.333
No. Wait a minute, this is crazy.

06:59.912 --> 07:01.004
You first.

07:01.480 --> 07:04.449
There's gotta be a way for you all
to enjoy the trophy.

07:05.684 --> 07:08.619
Wait a minute! I got it! No, lost it.
There it is again!

07:09.054 --> 07:11.147
Perfect, Peter.
Now we can all enjoy it.

07:13.726 --> 07:15.591
Here's to togetherness!

07:17.329 --> 07:18.353
Car!

07:22.034 --> 07:23.501
Meg, order up!

07:23.669 --> 07:26.331
Here you go, hon. From Flappy himself.

07:26.672 --> 07:29.766
I don't care if they're
from Kubla filthy-wretched Khan!

07:29.875 --> 07:31.570
Try them. You'll like them.

07:31.677 --> 07:33.907
Yes, well, I rather doubt that.

07:35.347 --> 07:37.872
Yes! These are delectable.

07:38.417 --> 07:41.682
Flappy, good news!
I've decided not to kill you!

07:44.256 --> 07:46.315
What a precious little boy.

07:46.425 --> 07:48.120
That's my son.

07:48.227 --> 07:51.025
Your son? But you're just a baby yourself.

07:51.130 --> 07:53.826
Henry, give the little skank a nice tip.

07:55.567 --> 07:56.556
$20!

07:57.636 --> 07:58.898
Welcome to Flappy's.

07:59.004 --> 08:00.904
Why don't you sit next to my baby...

08:01.006 --> 08:03.099
...whose deadbeat dad
doesn't pay child support.

08:14.219 --> 08:15.584
Peter, what is it?

08:15.688 --> 08:17.246
What's going on out here?

08:17.356 --> 08:19.221
Clear the way! I'm a cop!

08:19.325 --> 08:22.692
Oh, my God! I thought the safety was on.
I'm so sorry.

08:22.895 --> 08:26.422
That's okay, son.
It's your right as an American citizen.

08:28.067 --> 08:32.026
What's all the noise?
I was just jerked out of a sound sleep.

08:32.137 --> 08:36.699
Perhaps someone could enlighten me as
to the whereabouts of our Golden Clam?

08:36.809 --> 08:39.744
- Maybe it fell.
- Yeah. Right into someone's pocket.

08:39.845 --> 08:41.642
You think one of us stole it?

08:41.747 --> 08:45.615
I never said the word "stole." Looks like
someone has a guilty conscience.

08:45.718 --> 08:47.117
Guilty conscience!

08:47.386 --> 08:50.412
I'm the only guy on this block
who actually pays for his cable.

08:50.989 --> 08:55.483
Pretty high and mighty for a man
who left our nation's flag out in the rain...

08:55.594 --> 08:59.530
...last Fourth of July.
That's against the law, Officer!

09:00.799 --> 09:01.891
You're one to talk.

09:02.000 --> 09:04.525
Out there every trash day
picking through my garbage.

09:04.636 --> 09:06.035
That's an invasion of my privacy.

09:07.272 --> 09:10.241
He's sorting your recycling
because he loves our Mother Earth.

09:10.342 --> 09:13.072
If you weren't so busy
trolling for booty all the time...

09:13.178 --> 09:16.045
...you could do it yourself,
like the law says you should.

09:17.249 --> 09:18.216
It's on now!

09:18.317 --> 09:20.080
Wait a second! What about Peter?

09:20.185 --> 09:22.244
He's the one
who wanted the trophy all along!

09:22.354 --> 09:23.514
I couldn't have stolen it.

09:23.622 --> 09:27.388
Last night I was stealing Joe's ladder
so I could steal the trophy tonight.

09:27.493 --> 09:31.452
What? It's a ladder. He can't use it.
It's like taking a watch off a dead guy.

09:31.563 --> 09:35.431
Those Griffins always were oddballs, Joe.
Real oddballs.

09:35.534 --> 09:36.865
I don't trust them.

09:36.969 --> 09:39.597
I saw them taking coupons
out of our mailbox.

09:39.705 --> 09:41.502
I don't like the look of her!

09:41.807 --> 09:43.240
I offer you a recipe.

09:43.342 --> 09:47.108
Combine one small-town neighborhood
with a dash of missing trophy...

09:47.212 --> 09:50.340
...and what you're left with is a gumbo
fit only for a madman.

09:50.482 --> 09:53.042
A gumbo served almost exclusively in The...

09:53.152 --> 09:55.416
Who the hell is that?
I bet he took it!

09:55.521 --> 09:58.149
Where are you going, Serling?
Want some of this?

09:58.323 --> 09:59.654
Come back here!

10:03.495 --> 10:04.928
I'm off to work.

10:05.030 --> 10:06.088
Okay, honey.

10:06.198 --> 10:09.326
One of our neighbors took that trophy,
and I'll find out who.

10:09.668 --> 10:12.728
- I'm taking Stewie with me again.
- Fine, sweetie.

10:12.838 --> 10:14.806
This whole thing just makes me sick!

10:14.907 --> 10:18.001
- We played Pictionary with them!
- Bastards!

10:18.110 --> 10:21.602
Giddy-up, you stubby little mare!
To the pancake house!

10:22.748 --> 10:24.079
Well, bye.

10:24.183 --> 10:26.777
And to think
they used to be our best friends!

10:26.885 --> 10:28.750
That was then and this is now!

10:28.854 --> 10:32.847
And this is a chair. That's a lamp.
You have boobies. I'll find that trophy!

10:33.926 --> 10:37.555
To be honest, Peter, we were all
a little surprised you invited us over.

10:37.663 --> 10:41.895
We realized our friendship is a lot
more important than some stupid trophy.

10:43.068 --> 10:46.037
There's the tea. I'll get it, Lois.
Two sugars, right, Bonnie?

10:53.111 --> 10:54.669
Damn, it's not here!

11:06.291 --> 11:07.849
Not here either.

11:30.782 --> 11:31.976
Nothing.

11:36.154 --> 11:38.088
Oh, my God! We were robbed!

11:38.190 --> 11:40.658
- Is anything missing?
- No. I don't think so.

11:40.759 --> 11:43.227
Where's that picture of me
in my two-piece?

11:43.328 --> 11:44.693
Should I call the cops?

11:44.796 --> 11:47.526
I'm guessing a cop
had something to do with this.

11:47.633 --> 11:49.794
Or a pilot. Or a deli owner.

11:50.369 --> 11:52.098
Okay, you dirtbags!

11:52.204 --> 11:53.899
This means war!

11:57.743 --> 12:01.543
Excuse us. We're having a small problem
with home security.

12:01.713 --> 12:04.876
Do you have those round metal things
that you bury in the ground...

12:04.983 --> 12:06.644
...and, when stepped on, they explode?

12:06.752 --> 12:09.016
- Land mines?
- Land mines.

12:09.121 --> 12:10.247
It was land mines.

12:13.225 --> 12:14.783
- Quagmire.
- Peter.

12:15.027 --> 12:16.517
- Cleveland.
- Joe.

12:16.628 --> 12:18.596
- Bonnie.
- Lois.

12:19.031 --> 12:20.430
- Cleveland.
- Lois.

12:20.632 --> 12:21.599
Bonnie.

12:21.700 --> 12:23.292
- Quagmire.
- Peter.

12:25.470 --> 12:26.459
Loretta.

12:27.005 --> 12:28.495
Come on, Peter.

12:29.274 --> 12:30.832
That ought to slow them down.

12:33.111 --> 12:34.738
Being a single mother is hard.

12:34.846 --> 12:37.679
The real challenge is having a baby
that's addicted to crack.

12:37.783 --> 12:41.514
- Right, Stewie?
- What's that? Yes. I love crack.

12:41.620 --> 12:44.282
I'm absolutely coo-coo for crack!

12:44.723 --> 12:48.750
This is the first time he's eaten something
other than dog food in three weeks.

12:49.127 --> 12:51.254
Here's your check. God bless.

12:52.130 --> 12:54.724
Here, Honey.
What's this? Blueberries?

12:56.068 --> 12:57.035
Oh, my...

12:57.169 --> 12:58.693
That's better than sex!

12:59.871 --> 13:03.363
And could I get that waitress' address?
I'd like to help her baby.

13:09.581 --> 13:10.775
What are they up to?

13:10.882 --> 13:13.248
Cleveland and Quagmire
are holding their positions...

13:13.352 --> 13:15.149
...but I haven't seen Joe all day.

13:15.320 --> 13:16.719
Freeze!
Dad?

13:16.822 --> 13:19.620
Careful.
There's a bear trap two feet to your right.

13:19.725 --> 13:22.523
Thanks, Dad.
Look out for your mother!

13:22.628 --> 13:25.392
There's a sandwich
on the counter, honey.

13:25.697 --> 13:28.894
Cleveland, these lobster traps
aren't going to catch any intruders.

13:29.001 --> 13:30.161
Yes, they will.

13:30.268 --> 13:33.704
I baited them with these plump
and tasty Fenway franks.

13:34.206 --> 13:35.935
Daddy, we got one!

13:36.875 --> 13:39.901
Fat boy smelled a hot dog.
Couldn't help it. Went right in.

13:43.682 --> 13:45.946
- Hello.
- Say, get the hell off...

13:46.051 --> 13:48.042
Hello, lips, legs, breasts, and ass.

13:48.253 --> 13:51.950
Yes. I was hoping I could ask you
about your neighbors, the Griffins.

13:52.824 --> 13:55.850
A bunch of card-carrying Commies
if you ask me!

13:55.961 --> 13:57.087
All right.

13:57.195 --> 13:58.719
No! It's not all right!

13:59.564 --> 14:00.656
Fat boy!

14:00.766 --> 14:03.234
The Griffins are not to be trusted.

14:04.403 --> 14:07.167
Those people are nothing
but vile, cheating, lying scum.

14:07.272 --> 14:09.433
And their carpet and drape scheme...

14:11.777 --> 14:13.039
No! No, I won't!

14:13.145 --> 14:15.375
Get that puree of loathsomeness
away from me!

14:15.480 --> 14:17.505
But you love mashed turkey and peas.

14:17.616 --> 14:18.981
I'm sorry. What was that?

14:19.084 --> 14:22.178
Sorry, I didn't quite catch that.
Did you just tell me what I love?

14:23.221 --> 14:27.089
Write this down, you toad-faced frump.
I love pancakes!

14:29.628 --> 14:30.856
Hi, little fella.

14:30.962 --> 14:33.089
Is Meg Griffin here?
No, she's not.

14:33.198 --> 14:35.462
Probably out scoring more rock.

14:35.567 --> 14:38.934
Sandy Balfour, Child Services.
We're placing this baby in a foster home.

14:39.037 --> 14:41.198
- What?
- For God's sake, feed me!

14:41.306 --> 14:43.672
Let me guess. All out of Puppy Chow?

14:43.775 --> 14:45.538
What an awful home for a child!

14:45.644 --> 14:48.112
How dare you! This is a wonderful home!

14:49.314 --> 14:50.872
Quagmire, you rat bastard!

14:50.982 --> 14:53.542
Come near my fence again,
and that'll be your head!

14:53.652 --> 14:54.676
Shut up!

14:54.986 --> 14:57.250
Honey, would you like some pancakes?

14:57.355 --> 14:59.516
Oh, yes! God, yes! Take me!

14:59.958 --> 15:01.118
Stewie!

15:06.064 --> 15:10.228
Next up is Meg Griffin,
sporting her stylishly cool, brand-new...

15:10.969 --> 15:14.097
A woman from Child Services
came and took Stewie!

15:14.206 --> 15:16.333
She said we fed him dog food!

15:16.908 --> 15:17.966
Dog food?

15:18.210 --> 15:20.405
Is that a real Prada bag?

15:20.746 --> 15:24.614
How in the world did you make $1,100
as a waitress in one week?

15:24.716 --> 15:26.047
It's easy...

15:26.151 --> 15:29.450
...when you're the unwed teenage mother
of a crack-addicted baby.

15:30.789 --> 15:33.883
Wait a minute.
Meg, when did you become a teenager?

15:33.992 --> 15:35.584
She's 16, Peter.

15:35.761 --> 15:37.058
You knew about this?

15:37.863 --> 15:40.024
Welcome to your new home.

15:40.132 --> 15:43.659
Baby Stewie,
say hello to your new brothers and sisters.

15:45.437 --> 15:46.665
Hola, Stewie.

15:46.772 --> 15:48.239
Ni hao, Stewie.

15:48.473 --> 15:49.770
Stewie.

15:49.908 --> 15:52.706
Good God!
I've been adopted by a Benetton ad!

15:56.515 --> 15:59.848
- I promise, it'll never happen again.
- I hope not, Mrs. Stevens.

15:59.951 --> 16:03.114
Because next time we won't
just take him away, we'll kill him.

16:03.889 --> 16:06.824
Let's see. Stanley, Starkweather, Stevens!

16:10.462 --> 16:12.362
So this is where babies come from?

16:12.464 --> 16:15.092
Yes, Chris.
This is where babies come from.

16:15.667 --> 16:18.227
You told me I came out of your vagina!

16:18.637 --> 16:19.604
Next!

16:19.738 --> 16:21.296
Hi. Yeah, we're the Griffins.

16:22.307 --> 16:26.437
- I'm sorry. I can't find your paperwork.
- Look harder! I want my baby back!

16:26.545 --> 16:28.877
Please, let me handle this.
The name's Griffin.

16:28.980 --> 16:32.643
We're the ones who fed dog food
to our crack-addicted baby.

16:33.985 --> 16:36.351
I never was any good
at dealing with the authorities.

16:38.590 --> 16:40.558
Don't worry. I know how to handle this.

16:40.659 --> 16:43.059
Are you aware you were going 50 in...

16:44.796 --> 16:46.991
I'm gonna have to ask you
to put your shirt down.

16:47.365 --> 16:50.027
Crap.
I get the one straight cop in Rhode Island.

16:52.103 --> 16:54.037
Damn it! I want pancakes!

16:54.372 --> 16:56.670
You people understand every language
except English!

16:57.175 --> 16:59.006
Yo quiero pancakes!

16:59.177 --> 17:02.203
Donnez-moi pancakes!
Click-click-bloody-click pancakes!

17:02.314 --> 17:03.474
Poor little guy.

17:03.582 --> 17:06.142
"Pancakes" must be street for "crack."

17:06.251 --> 17:07.912
Damn those parents of his.

17:08.019 --> 17:09.577
Sarah, forgiveness.

17:09.988 --> 17:12.548
Now, Stewie,
why don't you go play with the others?

17:13.725 --> 17:17.058
Stewie, come complete our rainbow!

17:17.262 --> 17:18.752
I've got a better idea.

17:18.864 --> 17:21.424
Let's go play
"swallow the stuff under the sink."

17:23.101 --> 17:24.534
You lied to them!

17:24.636 --> 17:28.470
You told Child Services that we steal
lawn mowers and cheat on our taxes...

17:28.573 --> 17:30.734
...and worship some guy named Stan.

17:30.842 --> 17:33.970
Actually, I said Satan. That's a typo.

17:34.079 --> 17:36.411
We didn't know who she was!
It's not our fault!

17:36.514 --> 17:38.379
No? Then whose fault is it?

17:38.483 --> 17:40.041
It's all of yours!

17:40.151 --> 17:43.882
You were all working together just fine,
but then you won that stupid trophy.

17:43.989 --> 17:46.924
You put some shiny hunk of metal
before your own friendships.

17:47.025 --> 17:48.253
Brian's right.

17:48.360 --> 17:52.956
We were so obsessed with that trophy,
we lost sight of what was really going on.

17:53.298 --> 17:56.495
- Now we have a real problem to deal with.
- That's right!

17:56.601 --> 17:59.798
Somebody tipped off the cable company
about our free Cinemax.

17:59.905 --> 18:00.963
Joe?

18:02.173 --> 18:04.437
And we have to get Stewie back!

18:04.643 --> 18:06.941
I remembered.
We're here to help.

18:07.045 --> 18:08.910
And we must get our baby back.

18:09.014 --> 18:11.244
Right on! Let's do it!

18:11.483 --> 18:13.110
Rock their world!

18:16.855 --> 18:18.015
Yeah! Come on!

18:18.156 --> 18:19.987
Let's go! We can do it!

18:20.725 --> 18:24.559
See kids? One day the world
is going to be just like our home.

18:24.663 --> 18:27.894
All races living together
in harmony and love.

18:30.168 --> 18:31.396
Pancakes!

18:31.603 --> 18:34.265
He must still be working the junk
out of his system.

18:34.372 --> 18:36.169
He needs hugs!

18:37.442 --> 18:38.670
Doorbell!

18:40.412 --> 18:43.677
We're from the One World,
One People Book-of-the-Month Club.

18:43.782 --> 18:46.080
Is there something missing in your life?

18:46.551 --> 18:48.849
You know, I just bet there is.

18:49.054 --> 18:53.081
Sarah, we have guests!
And one of them is a homosexual!

18:55.560 --> 18:56.686
They're in place!

18:56.795 --> 18:59.389
God, it gets me hot
when Joe lies to strangers.

18:59.497 --> 19:01.829
When I get him home,
I swear I'm gonna grease up...

19:01.933 --> 19:03.628
That's fine, Debbie. Go, Chris.

19:04.202 --> 19:05.760
Here we go, Dad!

19:07.505 --> 19:10.668
Stewie, would you like
to learn how to wrap a turban?

19:10.775 --> 19:12.902
Why don't you teach it to the Chinese girl?

19:13.011 --> 19:16.447
Or perhaps she can learn
after her people invade your country.

19:16.681 --> 19:19.514
Yee, would your people really do this?

19:19.651 --> 19:21.243
Try and stop them.

19:21.353 --> 19:24.516
And try and stop Pablo's people
from using drug money to buy arms...

19:24.622 --> 19:27.750
...from Li's countrymen,
who in turn sells them to Ura's people...

19:27.859 --> 19:30.726
...so they can ethnically cleanse
this nauseatingly diverse...

19:30.829 --> 19:33.491
...grab bag of genetic party favors
you call a family.

19:33.598 --> 19:37.090
So now you all understand, yes?
You all hate each other?

19:39.604 --> 19:42.198
Hosanna! It's the lesser of two evils.

19:42.540 --> 19:45.668
Hey, kids. I'm Santa Claus.

19:45.844 --> 19:47.402
Just practicing for Christmas.

19:47.512 --> 19:48.945
But you're white.

19:49.147 --> 19:51.843
Jack and Sarah told me Santa is Indian.

19:51.950 --> 19:54.009
Don't be stupid! Santa is black!

19:54.119 --> 19:56.553
Santa can't be black. We do not fear him.

19:56.688 --> 19:59.282
Cram it, Gandhi!
Santa is Asian.

19:59.391 --> 20:00.824
How can he be Asian?

20:00.925 --> 20:04.861
Santa doesn't drive his sled 20 miles
under the speed limit with his blinker on!

20:04.963 --> 20:07.261
Go back to your rice paddy, Mulan!

20:08.767 --> 20:10.826
Come on, Stewie.
We're out of here.

20:10.935 --> 20:12.630
Dance, puppets! Dance!

20:13.238 --> 20:15.172
Lois, we got him. It's all over.

20:15.273 --> 20:16.262
Careful, Peter.

20:16.374 --> 20:19.502
Joe and Cleveland can't stall them.
They're heading your way!

20:19.611 --> 20:20.669
Crap!

20:20.779 --> 20:22.110
Hold it right there!

20:22.213 --> 20:23.407
Or what?

20:24.749 --> 20:26.114
Don't shoot!

20:26.618 --> 20:27.915
Now shoot!

20:29.387 --> 20:32.015
So, we're terribly sorry
we broke into your home.

20:32.123 --> 20:34.717
But we just had to
get Stewie back somehow.

20:35.260 --> 20:36.989
That's a very long story.

20:37.095 --> 20:40.656
But we've grown attached to little Stewie.
Plus, the law's on our side.

20:40.765 --> 20:43.962
You people can kiss
the fattest part of my ass!

20:44.069 --> 20:45.366
We'll be back, Stewie.

20:45.470 --> 20:46.528
Wait!

20:48.139 --> 20:49.800
Is that a real Prada bag?

20:54.212 --> 20:56.806
I'd like to propose a toast to our neighbors.

20:56.915 --> 21:00.373
Sure they may be black, handicapped,
and a heartless sex hound...

21:00.485 --> 21:05.115
...but if they moved out,
some smelly Hawaiians might move in.

21:05.223 --> 21:07.987
- Hear, hear!
- Where's Quagmire?

21:08.093 --> 21:10.527
If it wasn't for him,
we never would have found out...

21:10.628 --> 21:12.391
...where Stewie's foster family lived.

21:12.497 --> 21:14.556
He said he'd distract the social worker.

21:16.701 --> 21:21.001
Glen, honey, I have a question for you.
What do you do for a living?

21:21.339 --> 21:24.433
I have a question for you, too.
Why are you still here?

21:24.709 --> 21:26.939
What the heck happened
to that trophy anyway?

21:27.045 --> 21:29.445
I guess some mysteries
are better left unsolved.

21:42.393 --> 21:44.088
Submitted for your approval.

21:44.195 --> 21:48.461
A family pet with the uncontrollable urge
to bury shiny objects in the yard.

21:48.633 --> 21:52.694
A shameful secret that nearly buried the
peace and civility of an entire neighbor...

21:59.344 --> 22:02.177
Stewie seems a little feverish
after his ordeal.

22:02.280 --> 22:04.510
And he keeps asking for pancakes.

22:04.616 --> 22:06.584
Let's just let him rest.

22:07.852 --> 22:09.979
Flappy, what have you done to me?

22:10.088 --> 22:11.487
It's so hot.

22:11.890 --> 22:13.187
Now I'm freezing!

22:13.291 --> 22:16.419
What I wouldn't do
for one syrup-soaked bite.

22:16.420 --> 23:17.420
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru